      },
      "worked": "Since $9^x=(3^x)^2$, treat the equation as a quadratic in $3^x$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(3^x)^2-5(3^x)+6&=0\\\\(3^x-2)(3^x-3)&=0\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $3^x=2$ or $3^x=3$; both are positive.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\log_3 2\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=1\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
